title: Keep some in your own notes.
pid: 243e3aee-4e80-435a-bc58-62671e87cba1
body: |2-
  To keep another's note is to subscribe to and override it.
  You can also subscribe without overriding,
  if you intend to follow their thinking however they structure it
  without (re)structuring it yourself,
  but it is natural to be able to edit
  what you keep of their thoughts.

  Your atom and the ones it subscribes to are fused.
  You see what your subscribee's write,
  and integrate some of it into your notes,
  and hide the rest.
